<!--
  Name pools for the Colors that carry no prefix.

  Namers_ColorPrefixes.xml gives the six prefixed Colors their au/ag/cu/xe/si/ti
  particle and records why the other eight have none. That absence is correct
  and stays. What was NOT correct is that those eight Colors drew vanilla names,
  so a Red was "Jenkins" and an Obsidian was "Rebecca". The absence of a prefix
  is the statement; the names around it should still sound like the caste.

  So: no prefix anywhere in this file, and a register per group.

    Obsidian   given name + patronymic. The tribes keep no houses, only fathers,
               so the family name is "<father>sson" or "<father>sdottir". That is
               the one gendered pool, done with nameMakerFemale on the xenotype -
               a field observed on vanilla XenotypeDef (CLAUDE.md, "Xenotype
               budgets live on genes"). Shared by RR_Obsidian, _Stained and
               _Ascomanni.
    Red        short given name + the shaft the clan is named for. Reds identify
               by origin (DESIGN.md 8b), so the family name IS a place, assembled
               from mining syllables. Shared by RR_Red and RR_Red_Ultraheavy.
    Pink       given name + the Garden that raised them. The fiction's Pinks have
               a given name and little else; a Garden name stands in for the
               house they will never have. Shared by RR_Pink and RR_Pink_Rose.
    Violet     its own softer pool, artists' names.
    White      } the highborn register the Golds use, unprefixed. Whites and
    Yellow     } Yellows sit near the top and were never given a particle.
    Orange     } the servant register the Grays use, unprefixed.
    Brown      }

  EVERY NAME IS TWO TOKENS: "[given] [family]". A three-token r_name is parsed by
  NameTriple as first-nick-last, which is what the prefixed Colors rely on; a
  one-token name (a bare given name, which would suit Pink best) is not something
  this project has verified against NameTriple.FromString, so it is not used.
  If a single-name Pink is wanted later, that is the thing to test first.

  NAMES ARE ORIGINAL. No character name from the books appears here. Given names
  are ordinary historical forms in the public domain (Norse for Obsidian, which
  the setting's tribes draw on; Latin and Greek for the highborn, reused from the
  existing pool; plain working names for Red). Family names are built from
  syllables.

  Structure mirrored from Namers_ColorPrefixes.xml in this folder, which was
  itself mirrored from Biotech's RulePacks_Namers_Xenohumans.xml (NamerPersonImpid)
  and uses RulePackDef.include the way Anomaly's RulePacks_Art.xml does.
-->
